tests/golden/check/ffi-callback-position.hero:22:59: error[ffi_type]: `installer` cannot return `(function(i32) -> ())` — a function type crosses the FFI boundary as a *parameter* only (§4.19)
tests/golden/check/ffi-callback-position.hero:23:26: error[ffi_parameter_type]: `slot` of `grab` cannot be declared `(function() -> ())` — an `@` parameter is C's out-parameter, so this asks C to WRITE a function value here, and a function value Heroes calls must be one this compiler emitted. Declare it `@slot: ptr` if the program only stores what C writes, and pass it back to C to be called
tests/golden/check/ffi-callback-position.hero:24:31: error[ffi_constant_type]: an `extern constant` cannot be declared `(function() -> ())` — a function value Heroes calls must be one this compiler emitted, and this asks the header for one of C's. Declare it `ptr` if the program only hands it back to C
tests/golden/check/ffi-callback-position.hero:26:15: error[ffi_field_type]: `(function() -> ())` cannot be a field of a `record` in an `extern` group — the header owns the layout, and it can hold a number, `bool`, `ptr`, `cstr`, or another record of the group (§4.19)
